{title: Victory In Jesus}
{key: G}

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]I heard an old, old story,
How a [C]Savior came from [G]glory,
How He gave His life on [Em]Calvary
To [A]save a wretch like [D]me;
I [G]heard about His groaning,
Of His [C]precious blood's a[G]toning,
Then I repented [Em]of my sins
And [D]won the victo[G]ry.

{comment: Chorus}
O [G]victory in Jesus,
My [C]Savior, [G]forever.
He sought me and [Em]bought me
With [A]His redeeming [D]blood;
He [G]loved me ere I knew Him
[C]And all my love is [G]due Him,
He [Em]plunged me to [G]victory,
Be[D]neath the cleansing [G]flood.

{comment: Verse 2}
I [G]heard about His healing,
Of His [C]cleansing pow'r re[G]vealing.
How He made the lame to [Em]walk again
And [A]caused the blind to [D]see;
And [G]then I cried, "Dear Jesus,
Come and [C]heal my broken [G]spirit,"
And somehow Jesus [Em]came and bro't
To [D]me the victo[G]ry.

{comment: Verse 3}
[G]I heard about a mansion
He has [C]built for me in [G]glory.
And I heard about the [Em]streets of gold
Be[A]yond the crystal [D]sea;
A[G]bout the angels singing,
And the [C]old redemption [G]story,
And some sweet day [Em]I'll sing up there
The [D]song of victo[G]ry.
